    {
      "title": "Adstock / carryover",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Advertising effect persists and decays over subsequent periods. **Geometric",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#adstock-carryover",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "adstock**: adstock_t = x_t + alpha * adstock_{t-1}, where alpha in [0,1) is the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#adstock-carryover",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "retention/decay rate (higher = longer carryover). Often truncated at a max lag",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#adstock-carryover",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "l_max (e.g. 4-8 weeks). Delayed/Weibull adstock adds a peak-delay parameter",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#adstock-carryover",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(theta) so the effect peaks days after exposure (TV, brand) rather than",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#adstock-carryover",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "immediately - used by Robyn and described in Google's carryover paper.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#adstock-carryover",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Saturation / diminishing returns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Each channel's response is concave: incremental spend buys less incremental",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#saturation-diminishing-returns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "outcome as the channel saturates. Common forms:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#saturation-diminishing-returns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Hill function (from pharmacology): response = x^s / (k^s + x^s), with",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#saturation-diminishing-returns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "shape s and half-saturation k. Used by Meridian and DeepCausalMMM.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#saturation-diminishing-returns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Logistic saturation: used by PyMC-Marketing; saturation_lam controls",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#saturation-diminishing-returns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Michaelis-Menten / exponential variants in other tools.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#saturation-diminishing-returns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Adstock is applied before saturation: transform spend → carryover → saturated",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#saturation-diminishing-returns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "response → linear coefficient.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#saturation-diminishing-returns",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Response curves and budget allocation",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The fitted saturation curves yield diminishing-return curves per channel. The",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#response-curves-and-budget-allocation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "optimizer reallocates budget so marginal ROAS is equalized across channels (move",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#response-curves-and-budget-allocation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "spend from saturated to under-invested channels until marginal returns match).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#response-curves-and-budget-allocation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "This - not the historical ROAS point estimate - is the decision-grade MMM output.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#response-curves-and-budget-allocation",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
