    {
      "title": "Incrementality & geo experiments",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Incrementality = the causal lift attributable to advertising vs. a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "counterfactual where it never ran (not the same as last-click attributed",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "conversions, which include organic/baseline demand).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Geo experiments (GeoLift / geo-lift) are the practical gold standard:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Markets (DMAs, regions, ZIPs) are randomized or selected into treatment",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(campaign on / spend change) vs control (held out).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A counterfactual for treated geos is built from control geos.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Synthetic control (e.g. Haus, Meta GeoLift): a weighted blend of control",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "geos that best matches the treated geo's pre-period trajectory.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "TBR (time-based regression) / CausalImpact: Google's Bayesian",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "structural time-series builds a counterfactual from control-market series and",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "returns lift with credible intervals.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Key outputs: incremental conversions/revenue, iROAS (incremental ROAS),",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "iCPA, and confidence/credible bounds.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Power / MDE: run a pre-test power analysis to pick test length, number of",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "geos, and the minimum detectable effect; underpowered tests produce",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "inconclusive lift. Account for delayed conversions (e.g. long",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "consideration windows) by extending the post-period.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Pitfalls: spillover/contamination between adjacent geos; too few or poorly",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "matched control geos; post-hoc tweaking of the analysis window (p-hacking);",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "ignoring effect size in favor of p-values; insufficient pre-period for the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#incrementality-geo-experiments",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Calibrating MMM with experiments",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "This is where the methods become one system. A geo/lift test gives a causal",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#calibrating-mmm-with-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "estimate for a channel; feed it back into the MMM so the model's belief about that",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#calibrating-mmm-with-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "channel is anchored to reality.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#calibrating-mmm-with-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "ROI/ROAS priors (Meridian): set each channel's ROI prior from past lift",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#calibrating-mmm-with-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "tests, benchmarks, or experiments; the Bayesian model shrinks toward them when",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#calibrating-mmm-with-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "the time series is weak/collinear.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#calibrating-mmm-with-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Likelihood-based saturation calibration (PyMC-Marketing",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#calibrating-mmm-with-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "add_lift_test_measurements()): each lift test contributes",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#calibrating-mmm-with-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "`{channel, x (pre-test spend), delta_x (spend change), delta_y (measured sales",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/da-22-marketing-mix-modeling/#calibrating-mmm-with-experiments",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "change), sigma (uncertainty)}` - effectively two points on the channel's",
